# rljade.msg - Jade, Miss Kitty's right hand (Cat's Paw, New Reno)
# Plain ASCII only: the English Fallout 2 fonts have no umlauts or typographic quotes.

{100}{}{(A young woman in a silk jacket sits down without being asked.) Jade. Miss Kitty sent me. Venuti squeezes the Cat's Paw the same way he squeezes you. Miss Kitty thinks two houses on Virgin Street could stop squeezing back and start pushing. Or one of us could eat the other. She'd like to know which you prefer.}
{101}{}{[Speech] Tell Kitty we refuse Venuti together. Neither house pays.}
{102}{}{[Speech] Let's merge. The Cat's Paw becomes part of the Garter, and Kitty runs it. ($3000)}
{103}{}{The Garter is big enough to take the Cat's Paw in. Kitty runs it, and we split.}
{104}{}{[Unarmed] Kitty sells to me for $1500, or Kitty gets hurt.}
{105}{}{Remind Kitty what her best customers say in our private rooms. She sells for $1500.}
{106}{}{[Sneak] (Say nothing. Tonight you spoil the Cat's Paw's whiskey.)}
{107}{}{(Tell Venuti where Kitty keeps her books.)}
{108}{}{I'll think about it.}
{109}{}{Kitty?}
{110}{}{I have a rival's books, and Kitty's friends are in them. She sells for $1500.}
{120}{}{(Jade smiles for the first time.) Two houses, one answer. Venuti will hate it. Miss Kitty will send word whenever the Desperado is planning something.}
{121}{}{(Jade holds out her hand.) The Cat's Paw is yours, and Miss Kitty is yours with it. She knows every girl in New Reno, and every girl knows her. Half of what comes through her door is hers. That was always going to be the price.}
{122}{}{(Jade stands up very slowly.) She'll sell. And she'll leave New Reno, and she'll open somewhere you can't reach. You just made the only enemy on Virgin Street who's smarter than Venuti.}
{123}{}{(Three nights later the Cat's Paw's customers are sick in the street, and the Cat's Paw closes its doors. Kitty will find out who did it. She always does.)}
{124}{}{(Somebody saw you at the Cat's Paw's back door. By morning all of Virgin Street knows.)}
{125}{}{(Venuti gets the books. The Mordinos take the Cat's Paw by Friday. A thousand dollars lands on your table, and the fee gets a little lighter. Kitty gets out of New Reno alive. She'll never forget whose name was on the note.)}

# Look
{300}{}{A young woman in a silk jacket who watches the door.}
{301}{}{Jade, Miss Kitty's right hand at the Cat's Paw. She speaks for Kitty, and Kitty doesn't let just anyone speak for her.}
